  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CRPM 2022-2026</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CRPM 2022-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Gender Budget Watchdog Network (GBWN) &#xe4;r ett n&#xe4;tverk av civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer fr&#xe5;n v&#xe4;stra Balkan och Moldavien som syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra civilsamh&#xe4;llets deltagande i policyprocesser och budgetprocesser i regionen genom att granska offentliga budgetar ur ett j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsperspektiv. 

M&#xe5;let med insatsen &#xe4;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra de offentliga &#xe5;tagandena f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegrerade klimat&#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder och &#xf6;ka den tillg&#xe4;ngliga finansieringen f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegrerade klimat&#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder i v&#xe4;stra Balkanregionen och Moldavien.

N&#xe4;tverket samordnas av Centre for Research and Policy Making (CRPM), en icke-statlig regional organisation/tankesmedja med s&#xe4;te i Skopje. Sida finansierar 20% av GBWNs totala budget och resterande 80 % finansieras av &#xd6;sterrikes utvecklingsmyndighet ADA.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gender Budget Watchdog Network (GBWN) is a network of civil society organisations throughout the Western Balkans and Moldova which aims at improving civil society organizations&apos; participation in policy and budgeting processes in the Western Balkans and Moldova by using gender budget watchdog reporting and networking. 

The goal of the intervention is to improve public sector commitments for gender sensitive climate action and increase the available funding to implement gender-integrated climate action in the Western Balkans region and Moldova.

The network is coordinated by Centre for Research and Policy Making (CRPM), which is an NGO/think tank based in Skopje with a regional perspective. Sida is financing 20% of the total budget, and the other 80% is financed by the Austrian Development Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of the intervention is to improve public sector commitments for gender sensitive climate action and increase the available funding to implement gender-integrated climate action in the Western Balkans region and Moldova.

The goals of the program is:

i) Increased visibility and international recognition of the work carried out by the Gender Budget Watchdog Network

ii) Increased capacity of civil society organizations to use gender budget tools to monitor climate change policy and finance

iii) Improved participation of civil society organizations in policy and budget processes by using gender budgeting tools for monitoring for increased government accountability, especially regarding resilience, climate finance, and gender responsiveness and inclusion in the policy framework against climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
